---
layout: layouts/staff.njk
staffPage: settings
staffTitle: Settings
staffHeading: Your <b>account</b>
---
{#- SETTINGS (mockup board "Settings, just you", the last step). The heading
   is your name, and Account is the board's rows — your address, the
   language you read the console in, what you can do, the record of who
   looked at what, and signing out — one line each, nothing about the
   ministry among them.

   THE MINISTRY'S TWO THINGS KEEP THEIR OWN TABS. The board had none: it
   wanted Settings to be just you. But API keys came back here on
   2026-09-27 (Chase: like Cloudflare's and GitHub's, under the name
   menu), and the ministry's published languages sit with them. They change
   what strangers' websites serve, so they are apart from you, a tab away,
   rather than mixed in the way they were ("Your language" used to sit on
   the Languages tab above the ministry's). -#}
<div class="tabs" role="tablist">
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="account"
          aria-selected="true" data-i18n="set.account">Account</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="languages"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="set.languages">Languages</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="keys"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="set.keys">API keys</button>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================= ACCOUNT -->
<section class="tab-panel set-you" data-panel="account" role="tabpanel">
  <div class="set-r">
    <span class="set-lbl" data-i18n="set.email">Email</span>
    {#- NO PASSWORD CONTROL, because there is no password: Access owns
       sign-in and sends a one-time code. The ADDRESS is the identity here,
       so a typo in it needs an administrator and a Cloudflare dashboard to
       fix unless this exists. -#}
    <form class="set-ctl set-email" id="setEmailForm">
      <span class="set-now" id="setEmail">—</span>
      <input type="email" id="setNewEmail" autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false"
             data-i18n-attr="placeholder:set.newEmailShort,aria-label:set.newEmail"
             placeholder="New address" aria-label="New email address">
      <button type="submit" class="ghost-btn" data-i18n="set.sendEmailLink">Send confirmation</button>
      <p class="set-email-note" id="setEmailNote"></p>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div class="set-r">
    <label class="set-lbl" for="setPrefLang" data-i18n="set.consoleLang">Console language</label>
    <div class="set-ctl"><select id="setPrefLang" class="lang-pick"></select></div>
  </div>

  <div class="set-r">
    <span class="set-lbl" data-i18n="set.canDo">What you can do</span>
    <div class="set-ctl role-tags" id="setRoles"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="set-r">
    <span class="set-lbl" data-i18n="nav.activity">Activity</span>
    <div class="set-ctl"><a class="set-link" href="/staff/activity/" data-i18n="set.activityLink">Who looked at what in your ministry →</a></div>
  </div>

  <div class="set-r">
    <span class="set-lbl" data-i18n="nav.signout">Sign out</span>
    <div class="set-ctl"><a class="ghost-btn" href="/cdn-cgi/access/logout" data-i18n="nav.signout">Sign out</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =========================================================== LANGUAGES -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="languages" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  {#- The MINISTRY's languages: what its widgets and forms are published in.
     Your own reading language is on Account. -#}
  <div class="set-row set-row-block">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3 data-i18n="set.publishedLanguages">Published languages</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control" id="setLangList"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================================================================ KEYS -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="keys" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  {#- THE MINISTRY'S KEYS, like GitHub's and Cloudflare's tokens (Chase,
     2026-09-27): a key belongs to the ministry, so a partner website's build
     does not stop the day the person who made it leaves. Each key reads only
     the parts it was given; they can be changed later without a new key. -#}
  <div class="key-create">
    <input type="text" id="setKeyName" class="key-name" maxlength="80" data-i18n-attr="placeholder:set.keyPlaceholder,aria-label:set.keyPlaceholder" aria-label="What is this key for?"
           placeholder="What is this key for?">
    <div class="key-parts" id="setKeyParts"></div>
    <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="setKeyAdd"
            data-i18n="set.createKey">Create key</button>
  </div>

  {#- Shown once, on creation, and never again — the database stores only a
     hash. Deliberately loud, because there is no second chance to copy it. -#}
  <div class="key-reveal" id="setKeyReveal" hidden>
    <h4 data-i18n="set.keyRevealTitle">Copy this now — it cannot be shown again</h4>
    {#- The variable name is a LABEL on the value, not a sentence about it:
        it is what the partner site's build reads, so it is the one thing
        whoever pastes this has to get right. Not translated — it is a name. -#}
    <span class="key-var">THAUMA_API_KEY</span>
    <code id="setKeyValue"></code>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="setKeyCopy" data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
  </div>

  <div class="key-list" id="setKeyList"></div>
</section>
